// Pulses at each sample instant: `out` is true for one execute at each
// instant and false otherwise.  The instants are `shift` plus a whole
// number of `period`s after 1 Jan 1970 UTC, so components with the same
// `period` and `shift` pulse on the same cycle, and a `period` of 1day
// pulses at 00:00 UTC.  This is the CDL `Logical.Sources.SampleTrigger`
// block.
//
// An instant takes effect on the first execute at or after it, the first
// execute included, and fires once, even when the clock moves backward.
// A late cycle that passes several instants pulses once.  Instants on
// consecutive cycles keep `out` true, writing a new value each time, so a
// component that acts when its input turns true, as `Toggle` does, sees
// one rise for them.  Such runs log a warning to the `hxComps` log at
// most hourly.  A `period` of 0 or less is a fault: `out` is false with
// status fault.
SampleTrigger: HxComp {
  // Time between instants.  It must be more than 0.
  period: Duration 1min

  // Offset of the instants.  Only `mod(shift, period)` counts.
  shift: Duration 0sec

  // True for one execute at each instant
  out: StatusBool? <summary, transient, readonly, output>
}

// The base spec for components that sample `in` at instants a whole
// number of `period`s after 1 Jan 1970 UTC, the instants of a
// `SampleTrigger` with the same `period` and no `shift`.  An instant
// takes effect on the first execute at or after it, with the value of
// `in` on that execute.  A late cycle that passes several instants
// samples once, an instant fires once, even when the clock moves
// backward, and a change of `period` restarts the clock.  The state is
// not persisted.
//
// A null `in` sets `out` to null.  An invalid `in` holds the value of
// `out`, with the status of `in`.  A NaN `in` with a valid status, or a
// `period` below 1ms, is a fault: `out` holds its value, or takes `in`
// before the first sample, with the status of `in` plus fault.  An
// instant that passes while `in` is null, invalid or a fault takes no
// sample.
SampledComp: HxComp <abstract> {
  // Input to sample
  in: StatusNumber? <summary, transient>

  // Time between instants.  It must be at least 1ms.
  period: Duration <minVal:1ms> 1min

  // Output
  out: StatusNumber? <summary, transient, readonly, output>
}

// Samples `in` at each instant and holds the sample until the next one,
// with the status `in` had then.  This is the CDL `Discrete.Sampler`
// block.  It has direct feedthrough.
Sampler: SampledComp

// Holds `in` from one instant to the next, with the status `in` had at
// the instant.  This is the CDL `Discrete.ZeroOrderHold` block.  In an
// open chain `out` is the same as for `Sampler`.
//
// It has no direct feedthrough in CDL, `y = pre(ySample)`, but it does
// not cut a loop: `out` is null before the first sample, so a loop
// through it starts only if another component in it gives a value from
// a null input, as `Add` does.
ZeroOrderHold: SampledComp

// Follows a line through the last two samples of `in`, one period late:
// from the instant of sample k to the next,
// `out = u[k-1] + (u[k] - u[k-1]) * (time - t[k]) / period`.  This is the
// CDL `Discrete.FirstOrderHold` block.  Until the first instant `out` is
// the first `in`.  Between instants `out` is updated every second while
// it moves.  `out` carries the merged status of the two samples and the
// unit of the last.  An instant with no valid `in` takes the last sample
// again, and a change of `period` restarts the line where it is, so
// `out` goes flat rather than jump.  Like `ZeroOrderHold` it does not
// cut a loop.
FirstOrderHold: SampledComp
